-- Row il-57. EXPECTED RED: five assertions, all failing, two about each of items 1 and 2 and one about item 3. The count (5) is declared in check.sh and in encoding.json.
-- Each states what the printed words need. Nothing here is edited to make it pass.
-- Item 1: the definition in section 6(ב)(2) is to describe the extensions the Law has (which section 6(ד2) counts as four), so its citing words are to point at what the target is, and to be complete on a day after Amendment 67 takes effect.
-- Item 2: section 51(ד) is to fix the date for the allowance of every subsection that gives it, so its citing words are to point at what the target is, and to be complete on a day after Amendment 67 takes effect.
-- Item 3: the pronoun and its verb are to fit every noun the paragraph's head names. The row does not say that a court would read the words otherwise (the green file asserts that the pronoun fits one noun); it says what the printed words do not do.
-- The day 10 November 2026 is after the first day Amendment 67 is read to take effect (1 April 2026, the builder's computation, fork D1) by more than seven months.

